To help you embed the map into your mapping software, we need to generate an HTML snippet that includes the map. Here’s how you can do it:

First, let's create a basic HTML snippet using the map ID 'GlobalMap':

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My Map</title>
    <style>
        #map {
            height: 600px;
            width: 100%;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="map"></div>
    <script>
        // Initialize the map
        function initMap() {
            var map = new google.maps.Map(document.getElementById('map'), {
                center: {lat: 122.4194, lng: 37.7749},
                zoom: 8,
                mapTypeId: 'roadmap'
            });

            // Add markers
            var marker1 = new google.maps.Marker({
                position: {lat: 48.8566, lng: 2.3522},
                map: map,
                title: 'Statue of Liberty - Northwest'
            });

            var marker2 = new google.maps.Marker({
                position: {lat: 41.9028, lng: 12.4964},
                map: map,
                title: 'Statue of Liberty - Southeast'
            });

            var marker3 = new google.maps.Marker({
                position: {lat: 122.4194, lng: 37.7749},
                map: map,
                title: 'San Francisco'
            });
        }

        // Load the map script
        window.onload = initMap;
    </script>
    <!-- Replace the following API key with your own -->
    <script async defer src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=YOUR_API_KEY&callback=initMap"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Google Maps API key. This HTML snippet will display the map with the specified markers and allow you to embed it into your mapping software.

